{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":34260496,"ns":0,"title":"Hadamard product (matrices)","extract":"In mathematics, the Hadamard product (also known as the element-wise product, entrywise product or Schur product) is a binary operation that takes in two matrices of the same dimensions and returns a matrix of the multiplied corresponding elements. This operation can be thought as a \"naive matrix multiplication\" and is different from the matrix product.","description":"Elementwise product of two matrices","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}